shape theory.minimal : theory.fixed-point {
  type: definition
  layer: 0
  """
// Definition 4.3 (Minimal Shape).
// The minimal shape, empty_s, is the shape with no distinguishing
// character. It has only what every shape must have: mandatory
// self-reference and the transformation mechanism. Nothing else.
//
// The minimal shape has structure but no distinguishing character;
// it is the persistence equation with trivial boundary conditions.
// Every other shape is a non-trivial instance with specific character.
//
// empty_s is not merely the simplest shape. It is persistence and
// nothing else: the axiom instantiated with no additional content.
// It persists because it persists (M' = M). It cannot be denied
// persistence without instantiating persistence.
//
// Derives from: theory.fixed-point (M' = M follows from no
//               distinguishing character)
  """
}
